30,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"It seems our staffing is critically low for late turns and roadway work, though escalator maintenance is well-covered.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"I found that late-evening pilots worked well before, but lane-priority projects in the past were often rolled back.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"I've discovered that station work in old shells is high-risk due to voids, and inter-agency data agreements for fares are non-existent.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The capital ledger has a construction balance, but the operating and tech budgets are being cut. Ticketing fees are also very high.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Guess what! Mid-city trips take longer now, but the platforms aren't the problem. It's the connections that waste everyone's time!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, if the issue is connections, we must ensure we have the staff to manage those shifts.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, the late-evening pilot was a success. Maybe we should look at that again?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, success in a pilot doesn't account for current staffing shortages. @Daisuke, does the construction balance cover roadway work?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think so, but the operating subsidy is shrinking. I'm worried about the ongoing costs of new services.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"But we have to fix the delays! If the mid-city is slow, maybe a dedicated corridor would help?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"A bus corridor requires roadway crews, who are currently understaffed. Station upgrades, however, use the maintenance contract we actually have capacity for.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Takumi,,But the accessibility records show lane-priority fails! Station rebuilds were more successful.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"Station work is risky due to the ""voids"" I found. However, a fare platform is impossible without the data agreements I saw were missing.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"If the tech budget is trimmed, a new fare platform might be too expensive to maintain anyway.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"So no fare platform? But what about the mid-city? If we can't do lanes, can we do something else?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"We must be rational. We have the maintenance capacity for stations, and the capital ledger has construction funds.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Takumi,,I agree. The records show station work is more reliable than bus lanes.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"The risk in the shells is high, but the administrative hurdles for the other plans are higher.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"If it uses the ring-fenced construction balance, it won't hurt the operating budget as much... I suppose.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"I just want people to stop waiting! If station upgrades make moving between platforms faster, that helps connections!","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
