55,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Given the staffing shortages in the late-turn pool and roadway crews, Candidate B and A are impractical. I vote for C.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"Candidate B had a good pilot, but the accessibility records prove Candidate C is the most likely to actually be completed. I vote C.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Candidate D is a non-starter due to the lack of inter-agency agreement. Candidate C is risky, but the most viable. I vote C.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I'm worried about the costs, but Candidate C uses the construction balance. I'll... I'll vote for C too.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"I really wanted to fix the mid-city, but if the lanes don't work and the stations help connections, then C is the winner!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
